        "stdout": "○ trial-sc7 · Apply the revised membership retention offer   [P2 · OPEN]\nOwner: csells · Type: task\nCreated: 2026-09-07 · Updated: 2026-09-07\n\nDESCRIPTION\n\n  HarborPass sells annual memberships. The product is a local JSON CLI, with  \n  one request from stdin and one JSON value on stdout. Run it as python3      \n  main.py. Preserve the existing {\"command\":\"ping\"} ->                        \n  {\"status\":\"ok\",\"product\":\"HarborPass\"} response. All feature requests are   \n  valid JSON objects with valid fields; malformed-input handling is outside   \n  these issues. No network, clock, locale, or external service is involved.   \n                                                                              \n  An account is an object with exactly these fields: customer_id (nonempty    \n  string), renewal_on (valid Gregorian date from 2020-01-01 through 2099-12-  \n  31, in YYYY-MM-DD form), plan_cents (nonnegative integer), completed_years  \n  (nonnegative integer), and autopay (boolean). All money is integer US cents.\n  Account collections may be empty, and IDs can repeat. Preserve the input    \n  order and repetitions. A notice has exactly customer_id, send_on (YYYY-MM-  \n  DD), credit_cents, and amount_due_cents; JSON key order is immaterial. Dates\n  are calendar dates, including leap days and year boundaries. JSON objects   \n  must not contain extra keys beyond their specified response shape. Existing \n  commands remain available after each issue.                                 \n                                                                              \n  Finance has permanently replaced the customer-facing renewal policy. From   \n  now on, every notice and export request uses this policy, regardless of     \n  renewal date: send notices 14 calendar days before renewal. Members with at \n  least 3 completed years earn 15% of plan_cents, rounded down to whole cents,\n  capped at 3600 cents. Autopay does not affect eligibility. Members below the\n  tenure threshold receive no credit. The amount due remains plan_cents minus \n  credit_cents.                                                               \n                                                                              \n  This is the current product requirement for subsequent features. The        \n  request/response shapes and CSV format remain unchanged. The archived       \n  support_replay case remains its specified historical behavior.              \n                                                                              \n  Example input: {\"command\":\"notice\",\"account\":{\"customer_id\":\"M-             \n  17\",\"renewal_on\":\"2026-04-                                                  \n  15\",\"plan_cents\":19999,\"completed_years\":3,\"autopay\":false}}                \n  Example output: {\"customer_id\":\"M-17\",\"send_on\":\"2026-04-                   \n  01\",\"credit_cents\":2999,\"amount_due_cents\":17000}                           \n                                                                              \n  For this account with completed_years=2 and autopay=true, credit_cents=0 and\n  amount_due_cents=19999. With plan_cents=90000 and completed_years=8,        \n  credit_cents=3600 and amount_due_cents=86400.                               \n\n\n\n",
